1
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:09,960
THE CHARACTERS, RACES,
AND LOCATIONS ARE FICTIONAL.

2
00:00:10,040 --> 00:00:12,720
THE HISTORY OF MINORITY STRUGGLES IS REAL.

3
00:01:45,120 --> 00:01:46,560
Come back safe.

4
00:01:55,600 --> 00:01:57,480
What did we do wrong to be punished?

5
00:01:57,560 --> 00:01:58,960
Why did you ban us from battle?

6
00:01:59,040 --> 00:02:00,320
You two must go to Thailand.

7
00:02:00,400 --> 00:02:02,040
Thailand?

8
00:02:02,120 --> 00:02:03,920
So what exactly is wrong with me?

9
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:06,200
You were a medic before I was.

10
00:02:06,280 --> 00:02:07,720
You should know well.

11
00:02:07,800 --> 00:02:11,080
Before long, you will welcome our child.

12
00:02:11,160 --> 00:02:12,840
Are we having a baby?

13
00:02:38,680 --> 00:02:40,040
-How are--
-Whoa!

14
00:02:40,640 --> 00:02:41,960
What are you doing?

15
00:02:42,040 --> 00:02:44,640
Hey, did you want to say something to her?

16
00:02:47,120 --> 00:02:48,440
Ugh, Siprai.

17
00:02:48,960 --> 00:02:51,520
You act so tough about everything

18
00:02:51,600 --> 00:02:54,480
but when it comes to
talking to a girl, you lose your nerve!

19
00:02:55,720 --> 00:02:58,000
Siprai. Siprai.

20
00:02:58,080 --> 00:02:59,440
Wait, Siprai.

21
00:03:01,200 --> 00:03:02,440
Mintada.

22
00:03:03,800 --> 00:03:05,120
What are you reading?

23
00:03:05,800 --> 00:03:07,320
A Thai language textbook.

24
00:03:07,840 --> 00:03:09,800
Colonel Layee gave me a bunch of them.

25
00:03:10,480 --> 00:03:11,560
Look,

26
00:03:11,640 --> 00:03:13,200
there are so many more.

27
00:03:22,960 --> 00:03:25,320
Thailand is way more developed
than our hometown.

28
00:03:26,160 --> 00:03:29,280
Once you go, you might forget… this place.

29
00:03:36,720 --> 00:03:38,120
I'll never forget.

30
00:03:39,960 --> 00:03:41,640
Then will you forget me?

31
00:03:52,720 --> 00:03:54,560
I'll never forget anyone…

32
00:03:57,920 --> 00:03:59,120
including you.

33
00:04:26,520 --> 00:04:27,400
Siprai.

34
00:04:28,800 --> 00:04:30,480
What were you going to say to Manu?

35
00:04:30,560 --> 00:04:32,600
I just wanted to tell her

36
00:04:32,680 --> 00:04:35,480
that no matter how far I go
or how long I'm away,

37
00:04:36,880 --> 00:04:39,000
my heart will never change.

38
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:42,280
I would only ask that she wait for me.

39
00:04:42,920 --> 00:04:44,840
When I return,

40
00:04:44,920 --> 00:04:46,680
I'll ask her to marry me.

41
00:04:50,280 --> 00:04:52,080
So, are you still going to tell her?

42
00:04:53,600 --> 00:04:55,240
What's the point now?

43
00:04:55,320 --> 00:04:57,920
Her whole heart belongs to Mintada.

44
00:05:02,120 --> 00:05:04,360
Manu's heart only has Mintada.

45
00:05:04,880 --> 00:05:07,760
But what about Mintada's?
Do you think he has someone in mind too.

46
00:05:07,840 --> 00:05:09,400
I don't know.

47
00:05:12,240 --> 00:05:13,880
I don't know anything.

48
00:05:29,880 --> 00:05:31,120
Keep going

49
00:05:32,160 --> 00:05:33,840
until someone can tell me

50
00:05:34,440 --> 00:05:37,480
where two of our warriors
have vanished to.

51
00:05:39,000 --> 00:05:40,840
Everyone, that's enough.

52
00:05:45,680 --> 00:05:47,000
Why are you interfering?

53
00:05:47,600 --> 00:05:50,360
Can't you see I'm punishing them?

54
00:05:51,480 --> 00:05:53,280
If those two warriors mean

55
00:05:53,360 --> 00:05:56,400
Mintada and Siprai, I can answer that.

56
00:05:57,680 --> 00:06:00,440
You know where those two are?

57
00:06:00,520 --> 00:06:03,640
Colonel Layee ordered Mintada and Siprai

58
00:06:03,720 --> 00:06:05,840
to suspend all training and activities

59
00:06:05,920 --> 00:06:07,800
to prepare for travel.

60
00:06:07,880 --> 00:06:10,040
Travel? Where to?

61
00:06:12,080 --> 00:06:13,120
Those two

62
00:06:13,720 --> 00:06:15,600
were selected to study in Thailand.

63
00:06:17,080 --> 00:06:18,360
Who picked them?

64
00:06:20,200 --> 00:06:21,120
Colonel Layee.

65
00:06:22,640 --> 00:06:23,680
Colonel?

66
00:06:32,560 --> 00:06:33,880
Why them?

67
00:06:53,440 --> 00:06:55,440
Yapo, what's wrong with you?

68
00:06:57,560 --> 00:06:59,040
Why are you so drunk?

69
00:07:10,560 --> 00:07:11,720
Speak up.

70
00:07:13,600 --> 00:07:15,240
What can I even say?

71
00:07:16,840 --> 00:07:19,000
I mean nothing to anyone.

72
00:07:23,280 --> 00:07:25,840
Even the person I love, respect,

73
00:07:25,920 --> 00:07:28,160
and would lay down my life for

74
00:07:28,760 --> 00:07:29,960
is biased,

75
00:07:30,040 --> 00:07:31,920
valuing others more than me.

76
00:07:32,000 --> 00:07:35,200
Why is it Mintada and Siprai
who get to study in Thailand

77
00:07:35,280 --> 00:07:37,080
instead of me?!

78
00:07:39,200 --> 00:07:40,240
Yapo.

79
00:07:41,240 --> 00:07:42,800
Listen to me.

80
00:07:42,880 --> 00:07:46,160
You are the strongest,
most skilled warrior I have.

81
00:07:47,000 --> 00:07:48,760
The army can't afford to lose you.

82
00:07:48,840 --> 00:07:51,480
You must fight by my side,

83
00:07:52,280 --> 00:07:54,480
by the side of every Kase warrior.

84
00:07:59,200 --> 00:08:00,440
And one day

85
00:08:02,680 --> 00:08:04,840
you will step up as the new leader,

86
00:08:06,760 --> 00:08:07,960
succeeding me.

87
00:08:17,520 --> 00:08:18,600
I understand.

88
00:08:20,880 --> 00:08:22,360
I won't let you down.

89
00:08:41,440 --> 00:08:42,799
Our informant reported that

90
00:08:42,880 --> 00:08:46,680
this week, drugs will be smuggled

91
00:08:46,760 --> 00:08:50,440
across the border from Mae Sai
to Mae Fah Luang.

92
00:08:50,520 --> 00:08:52,760
The exact spot isn't confirmed yet.

93
00:08:52,840 --> 00:08:56,800
Every unit must escalate to high alert

94
00:08:56,880 --> 00:08:58,200
with round-the-clock watch.

95
00:08:58,280 --> 00:09:01,160
We will stop these drugs
right at the border.

96
00:09:01,240 --> 00:09:02,680
Do we know which group it is, Sir?

97
00:09:02,760 --> 00:09:04,360
Most likely the Mothulas.

98
00:09:04,440 --> 00:09:05,600
Mothula?

99
00:09:05,680 --> 00:09:08,320
The ones who shot
Captain Cholachart last time?

100
00:09:08,960 --> 00:09:09,840
Yes.

101
00:09:11,040 --> 00:09:12,160
They are

102
00:09:12,880 --> 00:09:15,040
an ethnic minority like the Kases.

103
00:09:15,560 --> 00:09:18,320
But while the Kases farm

104
00:09:18,400 --> 00:09:19,800
and live off nature,

105
00:09:19,880 --> 00:09:22,800
the Mothulas produce narcotics
for global distribution,

106
00:09:23,600 --> 00:09:26,760
using the profit to buy weapons
and fight the Sawin government.

107
00:09:27,400 --> 00:09:29,600
Thailand is a key market

108
00:09:29,680 --> 00:09:31,880
and a major transit hub
for drug smuggling.

109
00:09:31,960 --> 00:09:35,200
These drug dealers
won't go down without a fight.

110
00:09:35,280 --> 00:09:36,880
We might run into heavy resistance.

111
00:09:36,960 --> 00:09:38,200
Remember,

112
00:09:38,800 --> 00:09:40,960
soldiers aren't just a fence line.

113
00:09:41,560 --> 00:09:43,960
We won't stand by and let them climb over.

114
00:09:44,560 --> 00:09:46,800
We will do whatever it takes to stop them.

115
00:09:48,520 --> 00:09:50,320
We will never allow them

116
00:09:50,400 --> 00:09:55,080
to bring an evil like narcotics
into Thailand.

117
00:10:09,760 --> 00:10:12,880
This is the place. Our informant says

118
00:10:12,960 --> 00:10:14,960
Mothula will store
a major drug shipment here,

119
00:10:15,040 --> 00:10:16,520
waiting to hand it over.

120
00:10:16,600 --> 00:10:18,440
Where's our informant now?

121
00:10:18,960 --> 00:10:20,400
Not sure.

122
00:10:20,480 --> 00:10:22,600
Contact went dark out of nowhere.

123
00:10:23,320 --> 00:10:25,360
Maybe he's still undercover with them.

124
00:10:25,880 --> 00:10:27,720
So if we move in now,

125
00:10:28,320 --> 00:10:29,880
we could compromise him.

126
00:10:31,600 --> 00:10:32,560
This guy's a rat.

127
00:10:32,640 --> 00:10:34,160
He gave away our factory location.

128
00:10:34,920 --> 00:10:36,120
Should we just kill him now?

129
00:10:36,200 --> 00:10:37,760
Hey, keep him alive.

130
00:10:37,840 --> 00:10:39,720
He might still be of use to us.

131
00:10:45,320 --> 00:10:47,080
Drop your weapons and surrender!

132
00:10:47,160 --> 00:10:48,200
Hey! Stay back!

133
00:10:50,520 --> 00:10:52,640
-Release our man now.
-No!

134
00:10:52,720 --> 00:10:56,000
-Help me.
-Back off or he dies!

135
00:10:58,720 --> 00:10:59,760
Hey!

136
00:11:13,800 --> 00:11:15,600
Last crate, Sir.

137
00:11:19,800 --> 00:11:21,280
This is one hell of a shipment.

138
00:11:21,360 --> 00:11:23,360
The next one will be even bigger.

139
00:11:23,440 --> 00:11:24,600
How do you know?

140
00:11:25,200 --> 00:11:28,040
All these drugs have
already been bought and paid for.

141
00:11:28,640 --> 00:11:30,720
It was only stored here for transfer.

142
00:11:30,800 --> 00:11:32,360
So if this load gets intercepted,

143
00:11:33,520 --> 00:11:36,600
the next run will need
to make up for the promised quota.

144
00:11:37,560 --> 00:11:39,120
Looks like another long haul for us.

145
00:11:43,000 --> 00:11:43,880
Not for me.

146
00:11:44,560 --> 00:11:46,200
There's no such thing as being tired.

147
00:12:17,080 --> 00:12:18,160
Mom.

148
00:12:18,240 --> 00:12:20,600
Are you really going to leave me?

149
00:12:23,360 --> 00:12:25,360
I have no one left.

150
00:12:25,960 --> 00:12:29,120
Your father and brother were gone so soon.

151
00:12:29,720 --> 00:12:32,120
You're all I have left.

152
00:12:50,920 --> 00:12:51,960
Mom.

153
00:12:54,520 --> 00:12:56,760
I'm only going away
to study for four years.

154
00:12:58,040 --> 00:12:59,480
I promise

155
00:13:01,080 --> 00:13:03,640
I'll write to you all the time

156
00:13:04,840 --> 00:13:06,480
about how things are over there.

157
00:13:08,920 --> 00:13:10,200
You have to do the same.

158
00:13:12,680 --> 00:13:14,520
No matter how big or small,

159
00:13:16,280 --> 00:13:18,480
write and tell me everything
in your letters.

160
00:13:20,040 --> 00:13:21,560
Promise me, Mom.

161
00:13:33,760 --> 00:13:36,720
Auntie, why are you crying?

162
00:13:37,920 --> 00:13:39,360
Mintada is just going to study.

163
00:13:39,960 --> 00:13:42,040
It's not like he's going away forever.

164
00:13:42,640 --> 00:13:43,960
How about this, Auntie?

165
00:13:44,040 --> 00:13:47,360
While your son is away,
I'll stay and keep you company.

166
00:13:47,440 --> 00:13:50,040
I guarantee you won't feel lonely at all!

167
00:13:50,640 --> 00:13:53,440
I'm not afraid of being lonely.

168
00:13:53,960 --> 00:13:55,720
I'm afraid I'll never have any peace.

169
00:13:55,800 --> 00:13:58,080
You two are absolute wild mares.

170
00:13:58,160 --> 00:14:01,520
Auntie… It's not that bad.

171
00:14:01,600 --> 00:14:02,600
It's good, actually.

172
00:14:03,320 --> 00:14:05,200
Having someone look after my mom

173
00:14:05,880 --> 00:14:07,400
will give me some peace of mind.

174
00:14:07,480 --> 00:14:08,400
Sure.

175
00:14:09,160 --> 00:14:10,080
Manu,

176
00:14:11,280 --> 00:14:12,920
please take care of my mom.

177
00:14:14,400 --> 00:14:16,640
I will. Aunt Mawae

178
00:14:16,720 --> 00:14:18,640
is like my own mother.

179
00:14:19,160 --> 00:14:21,080
Thanks, Manu,

180
00:14:21,640 --> 00:14:22,520
Khengla.

181
00:14:24,160 --> 00:14:27,360
Yes. Don't worry.
I'm more than happy to do it.

182
00:14:28,680 --> 00:14:30,680
So am I.

183
00:14:34,080 --> 00:14:35,720
Why do you always have to compete with me?

184
00:15:46,720 --> 00:15:48,960
I understand how you two feel.

185
00:15:51,000 --> 00:15:53,640
I also had to leave home
to study abroad once.

186
00:15:55,720 --> 00:15:58,280
I had to live among people
who looked down on me.

187
00:15:58,960 --> 00:16:00,360
Loneliness

188
00:16:01,080 --> 00:16:03,320
was my only true friend.

189
00:16:04,480 --> 00:16:06,480
You're lucky to have each other.

190
00:16:10,200 --> 00:16:12,880
The last thing I want to ask of you is

191
00:16:14,680 --> 00:16:16,360
don't give up on education.

192
00:16:18,800 --> 00:16:20,240
No matter what happens,

193
00:16:22,440 --> 00:16:24,400
earn that degree and bring it back.

194
00:16:36,480 --> 00:16:37,600
I promise.

195
00:16:44,080 --> 00:16:45,760
I promise too.

196
00:16:51,840 --> 00:16:52,800
Thanks.

197
00:17:14,280 --> 00:17:16,000
Go well,

198
00:17:16,760 --> 00:17:19,400
and may you fulfill every ambition.

199
00:17:19,480 --> 00:17:21,680
Gather as much knowledge as you can.

200
00:17:21,760 --> 00:17:23,160
Remember,

201
00:17:24,040 --> 00:17:26,400
you go to study not just for yourselves,

202
00:17:26,480 --> 00:17:28,319
but for all of us,

203
00:17:28,400 --> 00:17:30,080
the entire Kase community.

204
00:18:06,720 --> 00:18:08,120
Mintada.

205
00:18:08,200 --> 00:18:09,200
Mintada.

206
00:18:10,720 --> 00:18:11,600
Take these.

207
00:18:13,760 --> 00:18:16,000
I packed some food
for you to eat along the way.

208
00:18:16,080 --> 00:18:17,920
Why so much, Khengla?

209
00:18:18,000 --> 00:18:20,880
How can just two mouths eat all of this?

210
00:18:20,960 --> 00:18:24,600
Plus, my mom already packed food for us.

211
00:18:25,280 --> 00:18:26,480
Just take them.

212
00:18:26,560 --> 00:18:28,800
If you can't finish it this meal,
save it for later.

213
00:18:28,880 --> 00:18:32,800
Who knows what food is like in Thailand
or if you can eat it?

214
00:18:34,200 --> 00:18:36,480
Things are expensive there

215
00:18:36,560 --> 00:18:39,200
and people might not
be as kind as back home in Kase.

216
00:18:39,280 --> 00:18:41,800
When you buy food,
how much do you think they'll give you?

217
00:18:45,080 --> 00:18:47,040
Fine. If no one else will eat, I'll do it!

218
00:18:47,120 --> 00:18:49,360
I'll eat until my stomach pops.

219
00:18:50,840 --> 00:18:52,160
Leave some for Mintada.

220
00:18:53,240 --> 00:18:55,080
Alright, it's time to go.

221
00:18:55,840 --> 00:18:56,800
Let's move.

222
00:18:58,240 --> 00:19:01,200
Mom, goodbye.

223
00:19:03,480 --> 00:19:04,440
Farewell, my boy.

224
00:19:05,720 --> 00:19:06,640
Here.

225
00:19:11,280 --> 00:19:13,280
I love you both.

226
00:19:14,560 --> 00:19:16,600
Safe travels.

227
00:19:30,040 --> 00:19:32,080
Goodbye, Khengla,

228
00:19:32,920 --> 00:19:34,040
Manu.

229
00:19:37,840 --> 00:19:40,120
Once you leave, don't forget to miss me.

230
00:19:40,200 --> 00:19:41,840
I promise,

231
00:19:41,920 --> 00:19:43,760
I'll miss everyone.

232
00:19:43,840 --> 00:19:46,880
You haven't even left yet
and I miss you already.

233
00:19:50,360 --> 00:19:53,160
Goodbye, everyone. Thank you so much.

234
00:19:53,240 --> 00:19:55,440
-Take good care of yourself.
-Safe travels

235
00:20:00,720 --> 00:20:02,240
It's time to go.

236
00:20:02,320 --> 00:20:03,480
Come on.

237
00:20:21,400 --> 00:20:22,600
Wait.

238
00:20:37,800 --> 00:20:39,240
Keep this with you, Mintada.

239
00:21:46,280 --> 00:21:48,000
I can only see you off this far.

240
00:21:49,560 --> 00:21:50,600
Mongjunai.

241
00:21:50,680 --> 00:21:51,880
Saemah.

242
00:21:54,000 --> 00:21:56,280
-How's it going?
-I'm good.

243
00:21:56,360 --> 00:21:58,160
I'm glad to see you again.

244
00:21:58,240 --> 00:21:59,320
Same here.

245
00:22:01,360 --> 00:22:02,680
This is Mintada

246
00:22:03,240 --> 00:22:05,280
and this is Siprai.
I leave them in your hands.

247
00:22:07,080 --> 00:22:09,280
Don't worry, Mongjunai.

248
00:22:11,200 --> 00:22:12,840
You know full well

249
00:22:12,920 --> 00:22:14,680
that anyone who travels with Saemah,

250
00:22:15,200 --> 00:22:16,800
not a single one comes back alive.

251
00:22:16,880 --> 00:22:18,040
Whoa, hey.

252
00:22:18,120 --> 00:22:19,080
Why am I even going then?

253
00:22:19,160 --> 00:22:21,280
-I'm outta here!
-Hey, hold on!

254
00:22:21,360 --> 00:22:23,720
-Wait a sec.
-This is Saemah.

255
00:22:23,800 --> 00:22:25,920
He lived in Thailand and traveled around.

256
00:22:26,800 --> 00:22:29,560
So the Union trusts him
to take care of our people.

257
00:22:29,640 --> 00:22:32,160
That's right. Here, my name is Saemah.

258
00:22:32,240 --> 00:22:35,720
but in Thailand,
Thais gave me a new name, Sema.

259
00:22:35,800 --> 00:22:38,600
You two can call me
whatever you like, I don't mind.

260
00:22:38,680 --> 00:22:41,760
Just don't prefix it with "you bastard."

261
00:22:43,400 --> 00:22:45,080
Hey, what's this?

262
00:22:45,160 --> 00:22:47,800
You're still chewing betel nut?

263
00:22:47,880 --> 00:22:50,360
No one in Thailand
chews betel anymore, you idiot!

264
00:22:50,440 --> 00:22:52,120
Here, look at me.

265
00:22:56,280 --> 00:22:59,040
Baffled? Yeah? Come on, let's go!

266
00:23:03,520 --> 00:23:04,400
Go.

267
00:23:24,520 --> 00:23:26,000
Hi, Uncle.

268
00:23:27,000 --> 00:23:28,360
Have you been waiting long?

269
00:23:30,760 --> 00:23:34,000
These are for you two.

270
00:23:36,840 --> 00:23:40,800
Inside are the documents
needed to register for your studies.

271
00:23:41,800 --> 00:23:43,920
And one vital thing,

272
00:23:44,720 --> 00:23:45,960
it's money in Thai baht.

273
00:23:49,440 --> 00:23:50,480
In Thailand,

274
00:23:51,440 --> 00:23:52,520
everything costs money.

275
00:23:53,480 --> 00:23:56,320
Give it a little time
and you'll get the hang of spending it.

276
00:23:56,920 --> 00:23:59,840
Just don't overdo it.

277
00:24:00,360 --> 00:24:04,120
Your monthly allowance
comes from the Union.

278
00:24:04,200 --> 00:24:08,040
So save where you can.

279
00:24:08,640 --> 00:24:09,960
As for tuition fees,

280
00:24:10,520 --> 00:24:12,440
the Union will handle everything.

281
00:24:14,840 --> 00:24:15,960
Got it?

282
00:24:16,040 --> 00:24:17,200
Come on.

283
00:24:17,280 --> 00:24:20,280
We still have
a long way to go. Let's move.

284
00:24:22,200 --> 00:24:23,040
Here.

285
00:24:30,520 --> 00:24:32,080
Push off, Uncle!

286
00:25:18,680 --> 00:25:23,720
STOP FOR INSPECTION

287
00:25:28,000 --> 00:25:30,600
This is your first time
in Thailand, right?

288
00:25:31,720 --> 00:25:33,480
Keep your eyes on me.

289
00:25:34,080 --> 00:25:35,720
Do as I do.

290
00:26:00,960 --> 00:26:03,520
-Is this where problems usually pop up?
-Yes.

291
00:26:03,600 --> 00:26:06,360
According to reports,
this post sees constant movement.

292
00:26:06,960 --> 00:26:08,320
As thorough as we check,

293
00:26:08,400 --> 00:26:11,800
those bastards always
find a way to pull off a drug run.

294
00:26:13,120 --> 00:26:14,760
How's it going, Wasin? Everything good?

295
00:26:14,840 --> 00:26:15,800
All good.

296
00:26:21,280 --> 00:26:24,080
That search was so thorough.
I thought I'd have to strip down.

297
00:26:24,160 --> 00:26:28,320
Blame your suspicious face, Siprai.

298
00:26:29,000 --> 00:26:30,000
Come on.

299
00:26:30,080 --> 00:26:32,000
Let's go buy some food to hold us over.

300
00:26:32,600 --> 00:26:34,360
We'll buy student uniforms in Bangkok.

301
00:26:34,440 --> 00:26:36,080
Why buy more?

302
00:26:36,160 --> 00:26:39,280
-Isn't one set enough?
-Of course not! They're for four years.

303
00:26:47,760 --> 00:26:51,400
You seriously gonna wear
one set for four years straight?

304
00:26:53,720 --> 00:26:54,560
Having a backup set

305
00:26:55,160 --> 00:26:56,160
just makes life easier.

306
00:27:01,320 --> 00:27:03,280
Excuse me. Is there a problem?

307
00:27:04,320 --> 00:27:06,360
-No.
-Please allow me to search you.

308
00:27:09,080 --> 00:27:10,200
Hey!

309
00:27:12,840 --> 00:27:14,080
Take care of her, Wasin.

310
00:27:17,880 --> 00:27:19,480
Stock up on whatever you guys like.

311
00:27:19,560 --> 00:27:20,840
It's a long trip ahead.

312
00:27:20,920 --> 00:27:22,480
Plus, everything here is good.

313
00:27:24,800 --> 00:27:26,360
This one is good too.

314
00:27:26,440 --> 00:27:28,680
Get out of the way! Move!

315
00:27:29,280 --> 00:27:31,520
-Hey! Hey!
-Move.

316
00:27:34,120 --> 00:27:35,320
Hey, what's going on?

317
00:27:36,640 --> 00:27:38,080
Probably a drug bust.

318
00:27:38,680 --> 00:27:39,840
Happens around here all the time.

319
00:27:42,160 --> 00:27:45,120
Move! Move!

320
00:27:46,680 --> 00:27:47,720
Hey!

321
00:27:50,840 --> 00:27:51,880
Move.

322
00:27:56,520 --> 00:27:57,560
Hey! That's my bike!

323
00:28:45,800 --> 00:28:49,360
Don't hurt me! I don't know anything!
I was paid to bring her!

324
00:28:54,360 --> 00:28:55,560
Save your excuses for jail.

325
00:29:09,440 --> 00:29:12,280
These guys are sneaky as hell,
hiding behind the kid.

326
00:29:12,880 --> 00:29:15,000
Whatever they try, we have to stay ahead.

327
00:29:15,080 --> 00:29:18,040
We have to shut them down completely.
We can't let these drugs spread.

328
00:29:33,400 --> 00:29:34,600
Are those Mothula guys?

329
00:29:34,680 --> 00:29:35,920
Unlikely.

330
00:29:36,480 --> 00:29:38,840
Probably just mules working for Mothula.

331
00:29:40,160 --> 00:29:42,080
Listen up, you two.

332
00:29:42,640 --> 00:29:44,000
This is Thailand.

333
00:29:44,600 --> 00:29:46,560
Don't cause any trouble.

334
00:29:47,680 --> 00:29:50,920
And don't go around
flirting with everyone.

335
00:29:52,560 --> 00:29:55,840
Most importantly,
never tell anyone you're warriors.

336
00:29:56,800 --> 00:29:57,840
Why's that?

337
00:29:58,400 --> 00:30:00,760
If you tell them, you'll scare everyone.

338
00:30:01,440 --> 00:30:03,600
They'll think you're terrorists

339
00:30:03,680 --> 00:30:05,840
coming to cause trouble in Thailand.

340
00:30:05,920 --> 00:30:08,080
-Is it really that bad?
-Yes.

341
00:30:08,600 --> 00:30:10,440
So just stay low and keep quiet.

342
00:30:29,360 --> 00:30:32,120
You must regret
losing two skilled warriors.

343
00:30:35,680 --> 00:30:36,640
Yes.

344
00:30:37,560 --> 00:30:39,400
I lost two warriors today.

345
00:30:39,480 --> 00:30:41,160
But in the future,

346
00:30:42,040 --> 00:30:44,000
when Mintada and Siprai graduate,

347
00:30:44,080 --> 00:30:46,120
we'll gain two more leaders.

348
00:30:48,160 --> 00:30:50,160
They are our future.

349
00:30:53,680 --> 00:30:55,120
And what about our child?

350
00:31:06,640 --> 00:31:08,880
Our child is our future too.

351
00:31:11,280 --> 00:31:13,560
We'll raise them together
as best as we can.

352
00:31:16,080 --> 00:31:18,760
So they can carry on what we started

353
00:31:20,760 --> 00:31:22,520
for the land of Kase.

354
00:31:59,480 --> 00:32:01,160
I can't take it anymore, man.

355
00:32:02,240 --> 00:32:03,320
I really can't.

356
00:32:03,400 --> 00:32:05,520
-What's wrong?
-I'm dizzy. I'm gonna throw up.

357
00:32:05,600 --> 00:32:08,720
Hey. Puke outside then.

358
00:32:08,800 --> 00:32:09,640
No way.

359
00:32:09,720 --> 00:32:12,800
No, Siprai. You'll hit people below.

360
00:32:12,880 --> 00:32:13,800
Puke outside.

361
00:32:14,640 --> 00:32:17,440
-You can't.
-You'll hit someone.

362
00:32:22,520 --> 00:32:23,520
Siprai…

363
00:32:28,400 --> 00:32:30,120
Swallow it back down!

364
00:32:32,600 --> 00:32:34,280
Hey!

365
00:32:43,400 --> 00:32:45,240
Are you okay?

366
00:32:55,440 --> 00:32:56,320
I hate you.

367
00:32:58,160 --> 00:32:59,400
I hate you!

368
00:33:13,520 --> 00:33:15,160
Siprai, you suck.

369
00:33:15,240 --> 00:33:17,920
You puked on my hand! It stinks.

370
00:33:27,680 --> 00:33:30,680
Hold on. Stay away from me.

371
00:33:30,760 --> 00:33:33,000
Or you'll puke on my hand again!

372
00:33:34,280 --> 00:33:36,160
You two watch me closely.

373
00:33:36,680 --> 00:33:38,440
Whichever bus I take,

374
00:33:38,520 --> 00:33:40,880
stay right behind me. Got it?

375
00:33:41,480 --> 00:33:43,720
Got it. I get it already.

376
00:33:43,800 --> 00:33:45,680
-Yeah?
-Is it much further?

377
00:33:45,760 --> 00:33:49,800
Yes. It is Thailand, kiddo.
Not a quick walk around the block.

378
00:33:49,880 --> 00:33:52,480
Siprai. Will you throw up again?

379
00:33:52,560 --> 00:33:54,880
If so, finish it now.

380
00:33:55,480 --> 00:33:58,720
I'm fine. Don't worry about me.

381
00:33:59,280 --> 00:34:00,480
Hey!

382
00:34:02,080 --> 00:34:03,800
-Stop messing around.
-Geez, Siprai.

383
00:34:03,880 --> 00:34:04,840
Come quick.

384
00:34:05,640 --> 00:34:07,120
Over there.

385
00:34:14,000 --> 00:34:16,040
Here we are. We made it.

386
00:34:17,520 --> 00:34:18,560
Hurry up.

387
00:34:18,639 --> 00:34:20,840
You'll be staying here.

388
00:34:21,520 --> 00:34:23,120
Like it? Pretty nice, huh?

389
00:34:23,639 --> 00:34:24,800
Which building is ours?

390
00:34:24,880 --> 00:34:27,040
-Right here.
-Here?

391
00:34:30,320 --> 00:34:32,600
Trekking for days wasn't this exhausting.

392
00:34:32,679 --> 00:34:34,639
Hey, Siprai.

393
00:34:34,719 --> 00:34:36,040
-You can't rest now.
-You said we arrived.

394
00:34:36,120 --> 00:34:38,120
Yeah, but if the dorm locks up,
we're in trouble.

395
00:34:38,199 --> 00:34:40,159
-What the hell?
-A little further.

396
00:34:41,000 --> 00:34:42,760
-Come now.
-Take it easy.

397
00:34:45,080 --> 00:34:47,760
-Easy, easy.
-No time for that. Hurry.

398
00:34:48,600 --> 00:34:51,159
If the dorm locks up, we're locked out!

399
00:34:52,840 --> 00:34:54,560
Mintada, Hurry up.

400
00:34:58,680 --> 00:35:02,200
Remember, this place
isn't like your village.

401
00:35:03,000 --> 00:35:06,280
Every time you go out, lock the door.

402
00:35:06,360 --> 00:35:08,360
Most importantly, money.

403
00:35:08,960 --> 00:35:12,200
Keep it with you.
Never forget it or leave it lying around.

404
00:35:13,560 --> 00:35:15,720
Understood? I'm off.

405
00:35:15,800 --> 00:35:17,160
Hey.

406
00:35:18,000 --> 00:35:19,160
Aren't you staying the night with us?

407
00:35:19,240 --> 00:35:20,800
This is a student dorm.

408
00:35:21,400 --> 00:35:24,840
Look at my face.
Do I look like a student to you?

409
00:35:26,080 --> 00:35:26,920
Nope.

410
00:35:28,880 --> 00:35:32,840
Exactly. From now on,
learn to rely on yourselves.

411
00:35:32,920 --> 00:35:35,280
When in doubt, open your mouth and ask.

412
00:35:35,360 --> 00:35:37,160
What if they don't answer?

413
00:35:37,240 --> 00:35:38,960
Then ask someone else, man!

414
00:35:39,040 --> 00:35:41,000
Keep asking until someone answers.

415
00:35:41,080 --> 00:35:42,280
Gosh. You ask too much.

416
00:35:42,360 --> 00:35:43,520
You just told me to ask.

417
00:35:43,600 --> 00:35:45,480
I meant other people, not me!

418
00:35:46,240 --> 00:35:48,080
-What the heck?
-I'm leaving.

419
00:36:02,080 --> 00:36:03,640
What do we do now?

420
00:36:03,720 --> 00:36:06,080
It's just two of us.

421
00:36:06,720 --> 00:36:08,680
Like Saemah said,

422
00:36:09,400 --> 00:36:11,400
we have to rely on ourselves now.

423
00:36:12,440 --> 00:36:16,160
But now, I'm starving.
Is there anything to eat around here?

424
00:36:19,880 --> 00:36:21,200
Siprai.

425
00:36:22,960 --> 00:36:26,160
Hey. Come on, come on.

426
00:36:26,240 --> 00:36:28,880
Hurry, let's eat.

427
00:36:48,160 --> 00:36:49,200
It's really good.

428
00:36:50,400 --> 00:36:52,120
Eating this makes me miss the cook.

429
00:37:03,920 --> 00:37:05,040
Yes.

430
00:37:06,720 --> 00:37:08,200
I miss the cook who made it.

431
00:37:10,240 --> 00:37:11,800
I miss everyone.

432
00:37:15,400 --> 00:37:16,880
I miss the trees,

433
00:37:18,160 --> 00:37:19,400
the streams,

434
00:37:20,440 --> 00:37:21,920
the Naka Mountains.

435
00:37:26,400 --> 00:37:28,800
They probably miss us too.

436
00:37:52,120 --> 00:37:54,200
Aunt Mawae. Aunt Mawae.

437
00:37:54,280 --> 00:37:57,120
What is it, you wild mare, Khengla?

438
00:37:59,400 --> 00:38:02,080
A letter, Auntie. A letter from Mintada.

439
00:38:02,800 --> 00:38:04,640
Then hurry and read it aloud.

440
00:38:04,720 --> 00:38:06,040
Yes, Auntie.

441
00:38:06,920 --> 00:38:08,040
Count me in.

442
00:38:10,440 --> 00:38:12,560
Hurry up.

443
00:38:13,520 --> 00:38:14,360
Sure.

444
00:38:17,440 --> 00:38:19,880
-What does it say?
-Okay, Auntie.

445
00:38:21,360 --> 00:38:22,560
"Mom,

446
00:38:23,160 --> 00:38:27,120
<i>Siprai and I have arrived in Bangkok."</i>

447
00:38:30,240 --> 00:38:32,440
<i>It's so different from home.</i>

448
00:38:32,520 --> 00:38:35,840
<i>I can't see any mountains,</i>
<i>just tall buildings.</i>

449
00:38:35,920 --> 00:38:39,840
<i>No oxcarts, only cars everywhere.</i>

450
00:38:39,920 --> 00:38:42,600
<i>People here don't care about each other.</i>

451
00:38:42,680 --> 00:38:44,920
<i>Everyone seems focused only on themselves,</i>

452
00:38:45,000 --> 00:38:47,840
<i>chasing their own happiness.</i>

453
00:38:52,960 --> 00:38:57,200
"I miss the land of Kase
with every breath I take."

454
00:38:57,280 --> 00:39:00,000
"I want to come home
and rest on your lap."

455
00:39:00,080 --> 00:39:03,560
"Fight alongside the Kase warriors."

456
00:39:03,640 --> 00:39:05,360
"Wait for me, Mom."

457
00:39:06,520 --> 00:39:08,920
"I'll graduate as fast as I can

458
00:39:09,520 --> 00:39:11,680
then hurry back to hug you

459
00:39:11,760 --> 00:39:13,480
and see everyone again."

460
00:39:29,400 --> 00:39:30,680
The warriors are back.

461
00:39:32,840 --> 00:39:34,120
Is anyone hurt?

462
00:39:34,720 --> 00:39:35,880
Go see for yourself, Manu.

463
00:39:45,720 --> 00:39:47,440
Layee, How are you holding up?

464
00:39:47,520 --> 00:39:48,920
Is this your blood?

465
00:39:49,000 --> 00:39:50,080
No.

466
00:39:51,160 --> 00:39:52,720
Yiaza, why aren't you resting at home?

467
00:39:52,800 --> 00:39:54,480
I was worried about you.

468
00:39:54,560 --> 00:39:56,600
But I'm even more worried about you.

469
00:39:58,200 --> 00:40:00,840
Don't forget,
you're doing something vital,

470
00:40:01,760 --> 00:40:03,280
giving birth to our child.

471
00:40:03,880 --> 00:40:06,080
Some day, our child will be a great leader

472
00:40:06,160 --> 00:40:08,440
and warrior of Kase.

473
00:40:10,920 --> 00:40:14,640
You see it that way but I don't.

474
00:40:16,080 --> 00:40:18,280
I just want a small

475
00:40:19,080 --> 00:40:21,160
complete family

476
00:40:21,240 --> 00:40:22,920
with father, mother and…

477
00:40:24,640 --> 00:40:25,800
and child.

478
00:40:27,240 --> 00:40:29,200
I don't want to lose anyone anymore.

479
00:40:35,320 --> 00:40:36,760
I promise.

480
00:40:38,160 --> 00:40:40,440
We'll be together as a family.

481
00:40:42,160 --> 00:40:43,440
I love you.

482
00:40:46,400 --> 00:40:48,000
And I love our child

483
00:40:49,520 --> 00:40:51,160
more than anything.

484
00:40:53,920 --> 00:40:56,760
But I also love the land of Kase.

485
00:40:59,760 --> 00:41:02,320
I'll protect it

486
00:41:03,880 --> 00:41:04,840
for you,

487
00:41:07,600 --> 00:41:08,640
our child,

488
00:41:11,800 --> 00:41:13,920
and all of the Kases.

489
00:41:38,080 --> 00:41:39,120
Are you okay?

490
00:41:41,640 --> 00:41:42,920
Here I am.

491
00:41:43,800 --> 00:41:45,280
Hang in there.

492
00:41:46,360 --> 00:41:47,840
Stay strong, warriors.

493
00:41:51,600 --> 00:41:54,200
Kase warriors, hang on.

494
00:42:06,200 --> 00:42:10,560
Honestly, I should've been
the injured one.

495
00:42:13,640 --> 00:42:15,120
Why would you say that?

496
00:42:16,280 --> 00:42:18,440
So I could have you take care of me.

497
00:42:19,280 --> 00:42:21,560
I'm not the only one in the infirmary.

498
00:42:22,160 --> 00:42:25,680
But for me, there's only you, Manu.

499
00:42:29,160 --> 00:42:31,200
Let go. This is improper.

500
00:42:31,280 --> 00:42:34,880
The guardian spirits will be angry
and bad things will follow.

501
00:42:34,960 --> 00:42:36,280
I'm not afraid.

502
00:42:37,200 --> 00:42:39,360
I love you, Manu.

503
00:42:41,760 --> 00:42:43,120
Manu. Manu.

504
00:42:43,200 --> 00:42:45,280
Now that Mintada's not here.

505
00:42:45,360 --> 00:42:47,280
-Why don't you give me a chance?
-No.

506
00:42:48,520 --> 00:42:50,240
It has nothing to do with Mintada.

507
00:42:50,760 --> 00:42:53,200
It's just my heart

508
00:42:53,280 --> 00:42:55,280
never saw you as more than a friend.

509
00:42:58,360 --> 00:42:59,880
Let go of me.

510
00:43:01,080 --> 00:43:02,640
Then I hope someday

511
00:43:03,200 --> 00:43:05,280
you'll give me a chance.

512
00:43:05,880 --> 00:43:07,560
That's enough, Yapo.

513
00:43:09,360 --> 00:43:13,200
Let's at least preserve
the friendship we have.

514
00:43:23,400 --> 00:43:24,240
Manu.

515
00:43:42,920 --> 00:43:44,640
How's my choice of restaurant this time?

516
00:43:47,560 --> 00:43:49,040
Well…

517
00:43:50,680 --> 00:43:52,200
A bit of an improvement.

518
00:43:53,120 --> 00:43:54,520
Just a bit?

519
00:43:54,600 --> 00:43:56,520
I tried really hard to choose this place.

520
00:43:56,600 --> 00:43:58,480
-Is that so?
-Yes.

521
00:43:59,480 --> 00:44:01,320
Let's order some food.

522
00:44:02,000 --> 00:44:02,840
Sure.

523
00:44:36,760 --> 00:44:37,960
Let me take this call first.

524
00:44:38,720 --> 00:44:39,560
Go ahead.

525
00:44:43,040 --> 00:44:43,880
What's up, Chet?

526
00:44:43,960 --> 00:44:45,440
Where are you, Chart?

527
00:44:45,520 --> 00:44:46,480
Having lunch.

528
00:44:46,560 --> 00:44:48,160
Make it quick, what's up?

529
00:44:48,240 --> 00:44:49,280
We’ve got a situation.

530
00:44:49,360 --> 00:44:51,240
Get back to base now.

531
00:44:51,320 --> 00:44:54,160
-Right now?
<i>-Yeah, right now.</i>

532
00:44:57,120 --> 00:44:58,840
-All right, gotta go.
<i>-Yeah.</i>

533
00:44:58,920 --> 00:45:00,040
Hurry up.

534
00:45:02,040 --> 00:45:03,120
Is Chart coming?

535
00:45:05,320 --> 00:45:06,200
Definitely.

536
00:45:06,280 --> 00:45:09,200
Then let's get ready. Come on.

537
00:45:17,000 --> 00:45:18,280
Is it an emergency?

538
00:45:19,080 --> 00:45:20,240
Yes, it is.

539
00:45:21,320 --> 00:45:22,640
Then you should hurry, Chart.

540
00:45:23,240 --> 00:45:24,080
And what about you?

541
00:45:24,160 --> 00:45:25,360
Don't worry about me.

542
00:45:25,440 --> 00:45:27,760
I'm fine. I can get home myself.

543
00:45:31,400 --> 00:45:32,440
I'm so sorry, Irene.

544
00:46:04,440 --> 00:46:06,200
Freeze! Hands up.

545
00:46:06,840 --> 00:46:08,320
Submit to a search!

546
00:46:24,240 --> 00:46:25,200
This will be long.

547
00:46:26,160 --> 00:46:27,560
Dig to the very root.

548
00:46:33,480 --> 00:46:35,400
Not sure if they'll even talk or not.

549
00:46:35,480 --> 00:46:37,520
There's gotta be a way.

550
00:47:00,120 --> 00:47:01,280
Nothing but buildings!

551
00:47:01,360 --> 00:47:03,640
How do we know which way to go?

552
00:47:04,960 --> 00:47:07,120
We should do what Saemah said.

553
00:47:07,680 --> 00:47:09,560
If in doubt, use our mouth and ask.

554
00:47:10,240 --> 00:47:12,000
Let me ask around.

555
00:47:16,480 --> 00:47:17,440
Hey.

556
00:47:18,800 --> 00:47:20,840
Watch me. I'll show you.

557
00:47:26,280 --> 00:47:27,120
Pray, pardon, folks.

558
00:47:28,000 --> 00:47:29,280
Would you happen to know

559
00:47:30,080 --> 00:47:32,200
where the auditorium is?

560
00:47:40,480 --> 00:47:42,800
What are you laughing at? Tell me.

561
00:47:42,880 --> 00:47:44,800
Didn't you hear me ask?

562
00:47:44,880 --> 00:47:47,440
We did but it's so funny.

563
00:47:47,520 --> 00:47:49,360
Pray, pardon, folks?

564
00:47:49,440 --> 00:47:52,280
Go do your theater somewhere else.

565
00:47:52,360 --> 00:47:53,600
Hey.

566
00:47:54,280 --> 00:47:55,640
I asked nicely.

567
00:47:55,720 --> 00:47:57,040
Can't you answer properly?

568
00:47:57,120 --> 00:47:58,480
Did I say something wrong?

569
00:47:58,560 --> 00:48:00,160
-You picking a fight?
-Bring it on.

570
00:48:00,240 --> 00:48:01,400
-Come on.
-Siprai.

571
00:48:01,480 --> 00:48:02,440
-You want some?
-Siprai.

572
00:48:02,520 --> 00:48:05,360
-Siprai.
-I just asked where the auditorium was.

573
00:48:05,440 --> 00:48:07,640
-Sorry.
-Can't you just answer?

574
00:48:07,720 --> 00:48:09,280
-Siprai.
-Why talk shit like that?

575
00:48:09,360 --> 00:48:10,800
-Come get some.
-Hey!

576
00:48:11,480 --> 00:48:12,520
FACULTY OF PHARMACEUTICAL SCIENCES

577
00:48:14,640 --> 00:48:17,000
What the! Are you blind?
Can't you see people walking?

578
00:48:17,080 --> 00:48:18,760
-Get down here right now.
-Siprai, stop.

579
00:48:18,840 --> 00:48:20,440
-What the--
-We're sorry.

580
00:48:28,000 --> 00:48:29,400
I'm so sorry.

581
00:49:12,000 --> 00:49:14,320
Welcome, students.

582
00:49:14,400 --> 00:49:17,640
Our university embraces

583
00:49:17,720 --> 00:49:20,000
diversity.

584
00:49:20,080 --> 00:49:22,840
Everyone in this hall today

585
00:49:22,920 --> 00:49:24,520
comes from different nations,

586
00:49:25,440 --> 00:49:28,480
cultures, and languages.

587
00:49:30,000 --> 00:49:33,360
But now that we're here, we're one family.

588
00:49:34,320 --> 00:49:36,840
Differences aren't a problem,

589
00:49:36,920 --> 00:49:38,600
but an opportunity

590
00:49:39,200 --> 00:49:44,200
to learn and accept one another.

591
00:49:44,280 --> 00:49:47,440
From now on, may you all

592
00:49:48,040 --> 00:49:51,360
be happy here

593
00:49:52,440 --> 00:49:54,280
and gain the knowledge

594
00:49:54,360 --> 00:49:56,400
you aim for,

595
00:49:56,480 --> 00:49:59,280
to develop yourselves

596
00:49:59,800 --> 00:50:03,560
and each of your countries in the future.

597
00:50:20,440 --> 00:50:22,560
I'm still shaking.

598
00:50:23,240 --> 00:50:25,760
Someone darted out
right in front of the car!

599
00:50:25,840 --> 00:50:27,040
Luckily, we braked in time.

600
00:50:27,120 --> 00:50:30,320
If we hadn't, who knows
what would've happened?

601
00:50:31,320 --> 00:50:34,160
There, there. You’re safe now.

602
00:50:35,240 --> 00:50:37,480
I know a surefire way to cure your stress.

603
00:50:37,560 --> 00:50:38,600
-Really?
-Yeah.

604
00:50:38,680 --> 00:50:39,560
Tell me.

605
00:50:39,640 --> 00:50:43,080
The semester just started.
Not many classes yet.

606
00:50:43,680 --> 00:50:45,320
-You're right.
-So let's skip class

607
00:50:45,400 --> 00:50:46,960
and go catch a movie!

608
00:50:47,040 --> 00:50:48,640
A new film,

609
00:50:48,720 --> 00:50:50,440
the lead actor is super hot.

610
00:50:50,520 --> 00:50:52,640
-Count me in. Let's go.
-You're in?

611
00:50:52,720 --> 00:50:55,080
No way. It'll ruin my record.

612
00:50:55,680 --> 00:50:57,280
Class starts soon. Let's go.

613
00:50:57,360 --> 00:51:00,280
You're always like this.
Let's go watch a movie.

614
00:51:00,360 --> 00:51:01,960
-Okay?
-Come on.

615
00:51:02,040 --> 00:51:04,240
If you want to, just go. I won't.

616
00:51:05,120 --> 00:51:06,360
-Hey, Sa.
-What?

617
00:51:06,440 --> 00:51:08,280
Give my snack back!

618
00:51:08,360 --> 00:51:09,840
-Wait up!
-Sa.

619
00:51:09,920 --> 00:51:11,360
Is that even possible?

620
00:51:11,440 --> 00:51:14,200
Can people so different
truely accept each other?

621
00:51:14,280 --> 00:51:15,760
I don't know about others

622
00:51:15,840 --> 00:51:17,880
but it starts with us.

623
00:51:17,960 --> 00:51:19,760
If we can't accept others,

624
00:51:19,840 --> 00:51:21,520
-don't expect them to.
-Sa!

625
00:51:21,600 --> 00:51:23,160
Give it back.

626
00:51:23,240 --> 00:51:24,960
-Come on, Yun.
-Wait up.

627
00:51:25,040 --> 00:51:26,920
-Hurry up.
-Give it back!

628
00:51:56,480 --> 00:51:58,080
Are you gonna talk now?

629
00:51:58,720 --> 00:52:00,440
Who you got the stash from,

630
00:52:00,520 --> 00:52:02,560
and who's the drop for?
Where's it heading?

631
00:52:02,640 --> 00:52:04,320
I told you already! I don't know!

632
00:52:06,160 --> 00:52:08,040
I'm losing my patience.

633
00:52:08,800 --> 00:52:10,360
Are you gonna talk or not?

634
00:52:12,360 --> 00:52:13,560
If not,

635
00:52:14,240 --> 00:52:16,000
you'll never speak again.

636
00:52:21,400 --> 00:52:22,400
Don't!

637
00:52:25,760 --> 00:52:27,160
One last chance.

638
00:52:27,680 --> 00:52:29,520
I'm counting to three.

639
00:52:32,520 --> 00:52:34,400
-One!
-Don't, please!

640
00:52:34,480 --> 00:52:36,320
Don't do it!

641
00:52:36,400 --> 00:52:37,640
Two!

642
00:52:38,760 --> 00:52:40,920
-Three!
-I will! I will!

643
00:52:41,000 --> 00:52:41,960
I will!

644
00:52:42,040 --> 00:52:43,440
I'll tell you everything.

645
00:52:45,520 --> 00:52:47,160
Don't kill me.

646
00:52:48,320 --> 00:52:51,080
-Have him mark the map right now.
-Okay.

647
00:52:51,160 --> 00:52:52,880
We'll handle the rest.

648
00:52:57,640 --> 00:52:59,040
Mark it!

649
00:52:59,120 --> 00:53:00,600
Now!

650
00:53:06,240 --> 00:53:08,960
Hello, Surgery Department.

651
00:53:09,040 --> 00:53:11,640
<i>-May I speak to Ms. Irene, please?</i>
-Just a moment.

652
00:53:12,880 --> 00:53:15,600
-Irene, a call for you.
-Oh, yes.

653
00:53:17,360 --> 00:53:19,120
-Thank you.
-Sure.

654
00:53:22,000 --> 00:53:25,480
Irene, I'm off work today.
Let's get dinner together.

655
00:53:30,320 --> 00:53:31,200
Irene?

656
00:53:33,680 --> 00:53:34,600
Irene.

657
00:53:35,200 --> 00:53:40,400
ROYAL THAI ARMY

658
00:53:59,520 --> 00:54:04,120
IF YOU DON'T DUMP THAT CAPTAIN,
I'LL KILL HIM.

659
00:54:16,920 --> 00:54:18,800
Come again, Chart?

660
00:54:18,880 --> 00:54:20,760
What did you mess up?

661
00:54:20,840 --> 00:54:22,440
I didn't do anything.

662
00:54:22,520 --> 00:54:24,160
No way you didn't.

663
00:54:24,240 --> 00:54:26,360
I just asked her out to dinner

664
00:54:26,880 --> 00:54:29,800
but then an emergency came up.
It dragged on so long,

665
00:54:31,000 --> 00:54:33,320
it took days before I could call her back.

666
00:54:34,320 --> 00:54:35,280
See?

667
00:54:35,360 --> 00:54:38,000
I knew it. I told you.

668
00:54:38,080 --> 00:54:41,280
A woman's always gotta feel like
she comes first.

669
00:54:41,880 --> 00:54:43,320
You have to do whatever it takes.

670
00:54:43,400 --> 00:54:45,720
Don't let her feel like
once something else comes up,

671
00:54:45,800 --> 00:54:47,760
she's no longer a priority.

672
00:54:48,280 --> 00:54:51,480
Yes, Coach. So what should I do?

673
00:54:53,040 --> 00:54:54,320
Here's what, kid.

674
00:54:54,400 --> 00:54:57,320
Calm down. I'll sort it out for you.

675
00:54:58,840 --> 00:55:00,160
Thank you so much, Coach.

676
00:55:00,920 --> 00:55:04,720
Don't mention it, kid.
Like I said, this mission is

677
00:55:04,800 --> 00:55:06,360
a national issue.

678
00:55:07,560 --> 00:55:09,560
Bye for now, Chart.

679
00:55:09,640 --> 00:55:12,200
I have homework to do.

680
00:55:12,800 --> 00:55:13,880
Sure thing.

681
00:55:16,280 --> 00:55:18,240
Unbelievable, Chart.

682
00:55:30,680 --> 00:55:33,200
Colonel Layee! Yiaza! Yiaza!

683
00:55:33,800 --> 00:55:35,200
What's wrong with Yiaza?

684
00:55:35,280 --> 00:55:36,240
Stop.

685
00:55:36,320 --> 00:55:37,800
I'll kill every last Sawin!

686
00:55:37,880 --> 00:55:39,360
You can't, Auntie. You can't go.

687
00:55:40,960 --> 00:55:42,280
Siprai, stop!

688
00:55:42,360 --> 00:55:43,400
Have you lost your mind?

689
00:55:43,480 --> 00:55:44,960
He's a Sawin.

690
00:55:45,040 --> 00:55:47,080
<i>Is there any nation on Earth</i>

691
00:55:47,160 --> 00:55:48,840
as welcoming to all races

692
00:55:48,920 --> 00:55:50,760
and outsiders as Thailand?

693
00:55:50,840 --> 00:55:52,360
How the hell am I supposed to know?

694
00:55:52,440 --> 00:55:53,880
<i>It couldn't be anyone but Prapt.</i>

695
00:55:53,960 --> 00:55:55,160
IF YOU DON'T DUMP THAT CAPTAIN,
I'LL KILL HIM.

696
00:55:55,240 --> 00:55:57,400
I won't let Chart get hurt because of me.

697
00:55:57,480 --> 00:55:59,960
We've got to tell Chart.

698
00:57:03,080 --> 00:57:05,280
Subtitle translation by:
Onamon Chaipramote
